  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In ChefLand, human brain speed is measured in bits per second (bps). Chef has a threshold limit of XXX bits per second above which his calculations are prone to errors. If Chef is currently working at YYY bits per second, is he prone to errors?\n\nIf Chef is prone to errors print `YES`, otherwise print `NO`.\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input contains two space separated integers XXX and YYY — the threshold limit and the rate at which Chef is currently working at.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nIf Chef is prone to errors print `YES`, otherwise print `NO`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `yes`, `Yes`, `yEs`, and `YES` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y≤1001 \\leq X, Y \\leq 1001≤X,Y≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "7 9",
        "output": "YES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef's current brain speed of 999 bps is greater than the threshold of 777 bps, hence Chef is prone to errors."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6 6",
        "output": "NO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef's current brain speed of 666 bps is not greater than the threshold of 666 bps, hence Chef is not prone to errors."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "31 53",
        "output": "YES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef's current brain speed of 535353 bps is greater than the threshold of 313131 bps, hence Chef is prone to errors."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_4",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "53 8",
        "output": "NO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef's current brain speed of 888 bps is not greater than the threshold of 535353 bps, hence Chef is not prone to errors."
      }
    ]
  },
